WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.220
- [Narrator] On China's
southeastern coastline

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:06.060
facing Taiwan is the
Huian military airbase.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:10.680
Since 2020, the airbase has
been significantly upgraded

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.110
with new hardened shelters,

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:14.433
an extended runway,

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.703
and a new apron for jet fighters.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:22.440
Huian is just one of at least
a dozen Chinese airbases

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:23.550
in southern China

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:26.763
that have seen infrastructure
upgrades in recent years.

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:30.360
Defense analysts say these changes

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:34.260
are part of China's preparations
for conflicts over Taiwan.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:37.050
The self-governing island
that Beijing claims

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:39.873
and has pledged to take
by force if necessary.

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:43.650
Here's how China has been
upgrading its airbase

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:46.120
to strengthen its military capabilities

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:50.910
and what challenges that poses
for Taiwan and its allies

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:52.623
in the events of a conflict.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:58.140
The Wall Street Journal
asked security analysts

00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:59.880
to study satellite imagery

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:04.880
of over a dozen air bases
within 500 miles of Taiwan.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.260
Alex Neill is a former defense analyst

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:08.520
for the British government

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:11.490
and specializes in Asia Pacific security.

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:13.860
- The modernization and the upgrades

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:18.860
of these air bases has
been specifically focused

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:23.550
on the ability to move air
assets to these airfield,

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:27.240
which are close to the
theater of of battle.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:29.430
- [Narrator] In its
biannual defense report,

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:32.070
Taiwan warned China's recent construction

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:34.140
at airfields along the coastline

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:37.140
is designed to seize air superiority

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:39.963
in the events of war
across the Taiwan Strait.

00:01:41.091 --> 00:01:41.924
(officer speaking in a foreign language).

00:01:41.924 --> 00:01:43.770
- [Narrator] China's air
force has been expanding

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:47.220
its spaces to accommodate a
wide range of military aircraft

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:49.773
ready for different types of combats.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:54.120
These upgrades can be seen
in the Longtian airfield,

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:57.720
one of China's closest base to Taiwan.

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:02.700
- Longtian airfield is
quite a special example of

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:04.260
the PLA'S modernization

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:08.340
because it not only has
an array of helicopters

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:09.450
and fighter jets,

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:11.250
at one end of the airfield,

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:14.820
you can make out camouflaged
hardened shelters,

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:17.880
which are housing UAVs.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:20.370
So large drones,

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:25.170
which can be in the air
reconnoitering the battle space.

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:27.840
- [Narrator] China has
developed supersonic drones

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:29.880
such as the WZ-8,

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:34.290
capable of penetrating deep
behind enemy radar systems.

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:36.210
A leaked paper from the Pentagon suggests

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:40.770
that WZ-8 drone is based
here at the Lu'an airbase,

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:43.320
and satellite imagery
shows significant upgrades

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:45.930
have taken place in recent years.

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:48.360
The leaked paper suggests
the upgraded basis

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:50.610
on China's southern coast would operate

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:53.160
as potential landing fields for the drone

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:55.623
during reconnaissance
missions over Taiwan.

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:03.390
China has been working on
the so-called survivability

00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:06.930
of its air assets in the
face of a retaliatory strike

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:10.320
by hardening the bunkers
where aircraft are stored

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:13.920
with layers of reinforced
concrete and steel.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:17.370
- If we look at a closeup
of this airfield here,

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:21.303
you can see hardened
shelters in this area,

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:26.580
so aircraft on the apron would be able to

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:30.210
advance quite quickly into
these hardened shelters

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:32.370
to refuel them to arm them.

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:34.470
- [Narrator] The purpose
of hardening shelters

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:37.650
is to ensure aircraft can
survive direct strikes

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.760
on an airbase,

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:41.280
allowing jet fighters to keep flying

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:43.200
once a conflict has started.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.320
- If there were an immediate
threat to the airfield itself

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:48.660
through missiles launched at sea

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.870
or indeed Taiwanese or U.S. aircraft,

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:55.470
it would be to able to
withstand a preemptive strike

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:58.173
or to have a second strike capability.

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:02.730
- [Narrator] A number of
the airbases like Anqing

00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:06.840
also have runways with direct
access to mountain bunkers.

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:08.340
- Under this mountain,

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:11.280
there will be munition storage facilities

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:16.020
as well as fuel and
potentially accommodation

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:19.860
for military personnel sheltering during

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:22.260
an attack on the airfield.

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:23.430
- [Narrator] The satellite images

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:26.640
show workers been undertaken
to harden the entrances

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:27.870
to these bunkers,

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:31.290
replacing exposed entrances
with what appear to be

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:34.920
reinforced structures topped
with a camouflage layer.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:38.640
Analysts say these changes are
part of China's preparations

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:42.303
to maintain its air force
in the event of a conflict.

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:46.170
The chinese military is also enhancing

00:04:46.170 --> 00:04:48.600
the survivability of its air bases

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:51.720
by constructing new air defense units.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:52.590
- If you look at this,

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:55.230
you can see this cog type configuration,

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:58.170
which has a perimeter fence
its own accommodation,

00:04:58.170 --> 00:05:01.710
hardened sheds for the missile batteries

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:04.080
and radar capabilities,

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:07.470
which would rapidly deploy onto this cog

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:09.338
to provide air defense.

00:05:09.338 --> 00:05:10.770
(military officers speaking
in a foreign language)

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:12.630
- [Narrator] Surface
to air defense systems

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:16.290
are designed to protect ground
positions from air attacks.

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:19.110
These systems are capable
of protecting airfields

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:20.700
from multiple threats,

00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:23.100
including high altitude bombers.

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:26.130
- So these air defense facilities

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:27.750
are not just for the airfield,

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:30.030
but they're more broadly speaking

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:33.870
a joined up chain of air defense.

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:35.460
- [Narrator] China's Ministry of Defense

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:37.170
didn't respond to a request

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:40.503
for comments on the recent
upgrades of its air bases.

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:44.850
U.S. officials say China's military

00:05:44.850 --> 00:05:48.510
is rapidly catching up
to Western air forces.

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:51.150
- [Neill] It's clear that
there's been a saturation

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:54.513
of this whole area with airbases.

00:05:56.970 --> 00:05:59.100
The united states and its allies

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:03.810
are also needing to use
their own geographical reach

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:07.203
in order to counter this saturation.

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:11.040
- [Narrator] If China
were to invade Taiwan,

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:15.420
Beijing knows it could spark a
wider conflict in the region.

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:18.390
- There's no doubt as demonstrated by the

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:20.820
hardening of these bases,

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:24.990
that the PLA military
leadership is aware that

00:06:24.990 --> 00:06:28.590
they will be big targets
for the United States

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:30.540
and Taiwanese forces

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:34.408
if there were to be
across straight invasion.

00:06:34.408 --> 00:06:37.158
(dramatic music)

